# Committed on purpose — these are NOT credentials.
#
# Vite loads .env.[mode] after .env, and `vite`/`vite dev` default to mode
# "development" — so Vite (the client) picks this up with no flag. The Express
# server is different: `node --env-file` doesn't know about Vite modes, so the
# dev script explicitly chains `--env-file=.env --env-file-if-exists=.env.development`
# (this file wins on conflicts) — see package.json.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here matters more than the anon key above: the
# server-side handlers (server/*.js) use it, and the service role bypasses RLS
# entirely. Pointing it at the local stack instead of .env's prod value is what
# stops a local `pnpm dev` from being able to read or write production data
# through /api/compose-paper and friends. .env keeps the values that are
# genuinely machine-local and unrelated to which Supabase project is targeted:
# PAST_PAPERS_BASE, PAST_PAPERS_DIR, SERVER_PORT, and the R2 credentials.
#
# Both the URL/key pair and the service role key below are the Supabase CLI's
# fixed local demo values — identical on every machine and meaningless without
# also holding a shell on this machine's Docker containers.
#
# To point local dev at something else deliberately (e.g. staging), create
# .env.development.local — both Vite and the --env-file-if-exists chain below
# load it after this file, and it's gitignored.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_ACJWlzQHlZjBrEguHvfOxg_3BJgxAaH
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6InNlcnZpY2Vfcm9sZSIsImV4cCI6MTk4MzgxMjk5Nn0.EGIM96RAZx35lJzdJsyH-qQwv8Hdp7fsn3W0YpN81IU
